  era: "499 CE \xB7 Section 10 \xB7 Gupta Empire \xB7 c. 319 \u2013 550 CE"
  title: Gupta-era mathematics
  text: The decimal place-value system with zero developed in India in this era. Aryabhata's Aryabhatiya, of 499 CE, gave a value of pi close to 3.1416 and methods in algebra and trigonometry. These ideas later reached Europe through the Arab world.
